#N canvas 20 20 2300 1300 12;
#X text 20 20 e_tape -- a held repeat's tails \, in c_kit (Brendan \, 2026-11-05): everything on c_kit's \$1-out \, the delays and the reverb \, is recorded all the time. While a repeat is held the recording freezes \, the last N steps of it loop in time with the replayed hits \, at a speed that follows the tempo \, like tape \, and the live sound is muted \, its engines ringing silently underneath. c_steps says when. ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 190 creation arg: c_kit's \$0 \, for a step's length \, \$1-step \, and the hits' sends \, \$1-gate. signal inlet: the wet sound \, c_kit's catch~. inlet: tape <span> <units> \, the replay begins: span ms of recording played in units steps' time \; off \, it is let go \; and run <1 or 0> \, rush's loop has it stop and go on. outlet~: the wet sound or its loop. The throws are never switched off: the voices' are zeroed at their own taps \, c_voice \, so no catch~ fills up., f 70;
#X obj 20 340 inlet~;
#X obj 900 340 inlet;
#X obj 900 380 route tape off run;
#X obj 20 500 *~;
#X obj 200 460 line~;
#X obj 20 700 outlet~;
#X obj 20 400 e_rec \$0 12500;
#N canvas 200 200 1400 950 play 0;
#X text 20 20 The player \, on only while a repeat is held. A delay line frozen by a switch~ does not read as a running one: delread4~ steps its head on by a block every block \, with the write head \, and inside the block counts back from the block's last sample. So what it is asked for a sample i of the block is the distance wanted less 63 - i \, from a table tabreceive~ reads every block \, and the head goes where the phase says (~/Sites/!reference/pure-data.md)., f 70;
#X text 20 180 Two heads a loop apart \, A and B. Over the loop's last stretch B fades in \, reading what came before the loop's start \, as A fades out \, and B reaches the loop's start as the phase wraps: there A takes over at that same place \, so the seam has no jump in it., f 70;
