#X text 20 780 The line holds 12.5 s \, four steps at the legal tempo's slowest with room for the seam \; c_steps keeps a span to 12 s. It costs its writing while it records and its memory always \, 2.2 MB., f 50;
#X text 20 920 At the replay's first step: the sends go to 0 at once \, before the step's hits \, and the recorder fades out over three blocks and is stopped. Its head is then 192 samples past the step's boundary \, so the loop ends 192 samples back from it \, and the player starts as if it had started on the boundary. Only then do the live sound and the loop cross over \, in 10 ms. A tape under a held repeat comes the same way: the loop fades out first \, since it jumps \, and in again., f 50;
#X text 1500 760 Let go: the sends come back and the live sound and the loop cross back in 10 ms. Only once the player is silent does it stop and the recorder run on from where it stopped \, fading in: a line being written moves under a head reading it. off during tape's 5 ms \, or tape during off's 11.7 ms \, cancels the other's delay \, and each path sets all it needs \, so any order of the two leaves the same state., f 50;
